          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "Only experimentally. Cypress's WebKit support needs experimentalWebKitSupport and the playwright-webkit package, and it lacks some features (for example cy.origin, Test Replay and forceNetworkError). Playwright supports WebKit as a first-class browser."
          }
        },
        {
          "@type": "Question",
          "name": "Which is better for API mocking?",
          "acceptedAnswer": {
            "@type": "Answer",
            "text": "For HTTP stubbing they're roughly equal. Playwright also replays HAR files and mocks WebSockets. Cypress has built-in delay/throttle and alias-based waiting. For shared mocks across tools, use MSW or a mock server."
